{
  "raw": {
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/123238": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow- MSO",
      "description": "Department: London Business School: Subject Area: Management Science and Operations Location: London, United Kingdom The Management Science and Operations (MSO) area at London Business School invites applications for a fully funded postdoctoral research position starting from the academic year 2023/2024.  The postdoctoral fellow will conduct research in Management Science and Operations, working closely with LBS faculty. The postdoc will be required to teach 37.5 hours (e.g., one half-term course to three streams) per academic year. Applicants must have completed a PhD before the appointment in operations management, operations research, computer science, applied mathematics, econometrics, or a related field.  They must demonstrate strong capabilities for conducting original theoretical or applied research using tools such as optimization, stochastic modelling, econometrics and causal inference, game theory, and machine learning. Ideal candidates must have a strong interest in how their research tackles real-world business problems, taken in a broad sense. The term is one year, extensible to two years, subject to continued satisfactory performance. We will offer a competitive salary and full access to the LBS environment. The postdoctoral fellow is expected to contribute and benefit from the resources of the MSO community, which includes interactions with faculty and PhD students, mentoring opportunities, organisation of reading groups, and training sessions. London Business School is an equal opportunities employer, and as such, we welcome applications from women, black and other ethnic minority candidates who are under-represented in our faculty. Please apply on Interfolio attaching your CV, three references, a research statement (up to 3 pages), and a sample research paper. You must also identify one faculty member in the MSO area at the London Business School that can act as your academic mentor. For questions about the application process, please contact Zainab Mehr zmehr@london.edu or Nicos Savva nsavva@london.edu We strongly encourage applicants to apply by 28 April 2023 for full consideration."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/129129": {
      "title": "Data Science Research Assistant",
      "description": "Department: London Business School: Subject Area: Management Science and Operations Location: London, United Kingdom The Management Science and Operations area at London Business School invites applications for a one-year full-time data science research assistant (RA) position.  The RA will contribute to research projects under the supervision of Dr. Ali Aouad on applying data analytics to digital platforms with application to the cultural sector. Previous research in this area includes a collaboration with the Van Gogh Museum, where the research team developed a predictive model of visitor trajectories from multimedia guide data (see working paper here ). The idea is to develop a dynamic choice model for cultural experiences (such as a visit to the museum or a session on a streaming platform) and apply it to recommendation systems and algorithmic curation. The RA may support other research projects, including analyzing a food choice dataset in a low-income community. We strongly encourage applications from candidates passionate about data science for social good who wish to pursue a Ph.D. after a pre-doctoral research experience. Applicants must have completed a BS/MS degree before the appointment in a data science field, which may include computer science, applied mathematics, econometrics, operations research, or a related field.  They must demonstrate capabilities for writing code (Python or R), basic knowledge in mathematical modelling, and prior experience using libraries in statistics, machine learning, or operations research. The position is funded by a research grant.  We will offer a competitive salary depending on qualifications and full access to the LBS environment. The RA will benefit from the resources of the MSO community, which includes interactions with faculty and PhD students, mentoring opportunities, access to research seminars, etc. London Business School is an equal opportunities employer, and as such, we welcome applications from women, black and other ethnic minority candidates who are under-represented in our faculty. Please apply on Interfolio attaching your CV and transcripts. We strongly recommend to provide a reference, and a sample scientific project and/or coding repository. For questions about the application process, please contact Zainab Mehr zmehr@london.edu and Ali Aouad aaouad@london.edu . Candidates are encouraged to apply as soon as possible. We will continue reviewing applicants until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/164191": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow- MSO",
      "description": "Department: London Business School: Subject Area: Management Science and Operations Location: London, United Kingdom The Management Science and Operations (MSO) area at London Business School invites applications for a fully funded postdoctoral research position starting from the academic year 2025/2026.  The postdoctoral fellow will conduct research in Management Science and Operations, working closely with LBS faculty. The postdoc will be required to teach 37.5 hours (e.g., one half-term course to three streams) per academic year. Applicants must have completed a PhD before the appointment in operations management, operations research, computer science, applied mathematics, econometrics, economics, finance, or a related field.  They must demonstrate strong capabilities for conducting original theoretical or applied research using tools such as optimization, stochastic modelling, econometrics and causal inference, game theory, and machine learning. Ideal candidates must have a strong interest in how their research tackles real-world business problems, taken in a broad sense. The term is one year, extensible to two years, subject to continued satisfactory performance. We will offer a competitive salary and full access to the LBS environment. The postdoctoral fellow is expected to contribute and benefit from the resources of the MSO community, which includes interactions with faculty and PhD students, mentoring opportunities, organisation of reading groups, and training sessions. London Business School is an equal opportunities employer, and as such, we welcome applications from women, black and other ethnic minority candidates who are under-represented in our faculty. Please apply on Interfolio attaching your CV, three references, a research statement (up to 3 pages), and a sample research paper. You must also identify one faculty member in the MSO area at the London Business School that can act as your academic mentor. For questions about the application process, please contact Zainab Mehr zmehr@london.edu We will review applications on a rolling basis until the position is filled but strongly encourage applicants to apply by 23 March 2025 for full consideration."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/127160": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Marketing",
      "description": "Department: London Business School: Subject Area: Marketing Location: London, UK London Business School is open for applications for tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor in the Marketing subject area. While applicants from all areas of research within marketing will be considered, we have a strong preference for a quant-oriented individual. The start date for this position is expected to start in August 2024, by which time candidates are expected to have received their Ph.D. First-round interviews will take place virtually via Zoom. Research and Teaching Requirements London Business School places a strong emphasis on both research and teaching quality. Faculty are expected to publish articles in leading academic journals. Career Progression The position is tenure track. Decisions about contract renewal and promotion are based on individual performance. London Business School salaries are competitive with those at top US business schools. Environment The London Business School Marketing Faculty’s research covers a wide range of interrelated topics. Current faculty members include Jonathan Berman, Simona Botti, Rajesh Chandy, Stephanie Chen, David Faro, Dafna Goor, Bruce Hardie, Oded Koenigsberg, Anja Lambrecht, John Mullins, Nicolas Padilla, Nader Tavassoli, and Xu Zhang. London Business School is a graduate school of the University of London, and a leading centre of excellence in management education and research. It has a central location in Regent’s Park in the heart of London. The School attracts outstanding students on its MBA, Masters in Finance, Masters in Management, PhD and executive programmes. Candidates will have a PhD, a developed area of research interest and some teaching experience. Business experience would be an advantage. For further information see http://www.london.edu/facultyandresearch/facultyrecruitment.html Candidates should submit (in PDF format): A cover letter Curriculum Vitae Three letters of recommendation A research statement A teaching statement At least one current research paper We will start the formal review of applications on July 3, 2023, and we highly recommend that you submit your application by 02 July at 11:59 PM Pacific Time Zone (PT). We will continue to accept applications until July 30, 2023. (Applications sent by post / courier or email will not be considered."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193291": {
      "title": "Affiliate Faculty positions at London Business School - OB 26/27",
      "description": "Department: London Business School: Subject Area: Organisational Behaviour Location: London London Business School is inviting applications for affiliate faculty to teach on the School’s master’s degree and Executive Education programmes starting in the 2027-2028 academic year. Courses may be delivered online or face-to-face, on our campuses in London or Dubai. Faculty teach in different formats, including standalone half-day or full-day sessions, 10-week courses that meet once per week or every other weekend, as well as 5-week electives. Our students range from those in our pre-experience master’s programmes (e.g., Masters in Management) to our MBA and Executive MBAs. We also offer open enrolment executive education courses. We seek exceptional and inspirational educators, and welcome applications from people from both academic and non-academic backgrounds. Successful applicants will teach in the Organisational Behaviour Subject Area. Candidates should be able and willing to teach a selection of management and leadership courses and sessions that may include topics such as negotiations and influence, teams, leading change, power, organizational transformation, culture, innovation, personality, interpersonal dynamics, or leading in the age of AI. A PhD in a relevant field is required, and we strongly prefer candidates with evidence of successful teaching to MBA, executive, and/or early-career audiences. The ideal candidate lives in or close to London, or is willing to travel to London on their own budget. Inclusion and diversity have always been a cornerstone of London Business School’s values and we particularly welcome female applicants and those from an ethnic minority, as they are currently under-represented within our faculty. Please apply on Interfolio attaching your CV, a cover letter outlining your area of expertise and teaching experience, as well as representative feedback from students/participants you have previously taught. You are also strongly encouraged to submit a video sample of yourself teaching."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190961": {
      "title": "PhD Programme in Accounting 2027",
      "description": "Department: London Business School: Subject Area: Accounting PhD Location: London The PhD Programme is London Business School's investment in the future of management teaching and research. Expert faculty, partnership opportunities, leading-edge research methods and close supervision contribute to an outstanding study environment. For further details please visit our website For further details please visit our website. Please complete the following: 1.  Application Fee (£75) The payment should be made here: https://www.london.edu/forms/phd-payment 2. Document upload Original GMAT/GRE score report (less than five years old at the time of the application) Statement of Purpose (1000-1500 words)* Final Transcript** CV A valid original Test of English as a Foreign Language (TOEFL), International English Language Testing System (IELTS) or Duolingo score report *Statement of Purpose You should describe your reasons and motivations for pursuing a PhD in your chosen field, noting the experiences that shaped your research ambitions, indicating briefly your research interests and career objectives, and concisely stating your past research experience/work in your intended field of study. Explain why you have chosen LBS, how the faculty, research, and resources here would contribute to your future research goals. **Transcripts Transcripts for all degrees undertaken should be submitted. For applicants submitting more than one transcript or test score please use the Additional Documents tool. 3.  Two academic references 4. Forms PhD Application Form PhD Reference Form Diversity Monitoring Form"
    },
